# ---- NEVER COMMIT GAME DATA -------------------------------------------------
# Refused rather than merely omitted: the accident should be impossible, not
# something a future contributor has to remember not to have.

# disc images and their sidecars
*.iso
*.bin
*.cue
*.img
*.ccd
*.sub
*.mdf
*.mds
*.chd
*.pbp

# the game executable, by every regional prefix
SLES_*
SLUS_*
SLPS_*
SCES_*
SCUS_*
SCPS_*
*.exe

# game assets
*.XA
*.STR
*.TIM
*.VB
*.VH
*.FOLIO
FOLIO*

# ⚠ CONSOLE BIOS. Not the game, still not ours to distribute.
scph*.bin
scph*.BIN
*.bios

# ⚠ SAVE STATES AND MEMORY CARDS ARE GAME DATA. A save state is a dump of the
# game's own memory with its code in it; a memory card is its save format.
# (tinyclaw's catch -- this list did not refuse either.)
*.sstate
*.state
*.savestate
*.mcd
*.mcr
*.srm

# ⚠ RAW DISASSEMBLY IS THE GAME'S CODE WEARING A DIFFERENT HAT. Bulk dumps of
# the executable are the executable. (tinyclaw's catch.)
*.dis
*.disasm
disasm/
disassembly/

# ⚠ NOT BLOCKED, DELIBERATELY: *.s and *.asm. A matching decomp legitimately
# commits extracted assembly -- that IS the workflow -- so a blanket rule here
# would refuse the project's own source. Raw bulk dumps are what the rules above
# are for; if an .s file ever holds a whole segment rather than one function,
# that is a review question and not something a pattern can decide.

# emulator trees and their unpacked contents
duckstation/
pcsx*/
mednafen/
bios/

# ---- build output -----------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
build/
*.o
*.elf

# build output
bin/
obj/
build/
*.o
*.elf
.vs/
*.user
findings/records.json
